  "nodes": [
    {
      "id": "e2c88d84-af71-4d4c-a0d8-f6f4f5d4e527",
      "name": "Sticky Note - Overview",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        0,
        0
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": "#FFC800",
        "width": 960,
        "height": 1128,
        "content": "## MCP Server → n8n → Production Tools\n\nExposes n8n itself as an MCP server: an MCP client (Claude Desktop, Claude Code, or any other MCP-speaking agent) connects to this workflow's MCP Server Trigger, sees a curated menu of tools, and calls them like any other MCP tool. Each call is validated, authorized, and audit-logged before it's allowed to touch a real production system - so the model never gets raw API/database access, only this pre-built menu, mirroring the allow-list pattern used for autonomous action agents.\n\nUnlike a single fixed pipeline, this fans out by tool name: read-only tools (status lookup, search) execute immediately, while destructive/write tools (deploy, delete, refund) are routed through a human-approval gate before anything actually runs against production.\n\n### How it works\n1. An MCP Server Trigger listens for tool-call requests from any connected MCP client.\n2. A Code node validates the incoming tool call: is the tool name on the allow-list, are the required parameters present and well-typed. Invalid calls are rejected immediately with a typed error - no production system is touched.\n3. If valid, the call is logged to the audit trail BEFORE execution, so even a crash mid-call leaves a record of what was requested.\n4. A Switch node routes by tool name/category: read-only tools go straight to execution; destructive tools go to an approval gate first.\n5. Destructive tool calls post to Slack for human approval and pause on a Wait node until someone responds.\n6. Approved destructive calls, and all read-only calls, are dispatched to exactly one real, narrow-scoped production API per tool - deploy service, query database, search knowledge base, restart process, issue refund.\n7. Every branch converges and logs the execution result (success/failure, response) against the original call.\n8. The MCP Server Trigger returns the tool result back to the calling MCP client.\n\n### Setup\n1. Import this workflow into n8n and activate it.\n2. Add your production system credentials to each Execute node (deploy API, database, refund/payments API, search/knowledge-base API).\n3. Add Slack credentials for the human-approval branch.\n4. Add a database/queue credential for the audit log store.\n5. Point your MCP client (Claude Desktop, Claude Code, etc.) at this workflow's MCP Server Trigger URL.\n\n### Customization\n- Add or remove tools from the allow-list in JS - Validate Tool Call without touching the execution nodes.\n- Tighten which tools require human approval by editing the Switch - Route By Tool Category rules.\n- Add a per-tool rate limit or cost budget check before execution for expensive production actions.\n- Feed the audit log back into future tool descriptions so the model learns which tools are safe to call more freely."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "5a349463-600a-4cdd-a1ac-6500366b8e74",
      "name": "Sticky Note - Stage 1",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        1024,
        112
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 3,
        "width": 920,
        "height": 956,
        "content": "## Stage 1: MCP Trigger & Call Validation\n\n- **MCP Server Trigger** — listens for tool-call requests from any connected MCP client (Claude Desktop, Claude Code, etc.) and exposes the tool menu.\n- **JS - Validate Tool Call** — checks the requested tool name against the allow-list and validates required parameters are present and well-typed; invalid calls are rejected before touching any production system.\n- **IF - Tool Call Valid?** — branches to logging + routing if valid, else straight to a typed rejection.\n- **Respond - Invalid Tool Call** — returns a typed error back through the MCP Server Trigger for a rejected call.\n- **JS - Log Call (Pre-Execution)** — writes the requested tool call to the audit trail BEFORE anything runs, so even a crash mid-call leaves a record."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "239aa1b4-3a81-4470-af37-6a98e89de772",
      "name": "Sticky Note - Stage 2",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        1984,
        112
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 4,
        "width": 856,
        "height": 740,
        "content": "## Stage 2: Routing & Human Approval Gate\n\n- **Switch - Route By Tool Category** — routes read-only tools straight to execution; routes destructive tools (deploy, delete, refund) to the approval gate first.\n- **Slack - Request Approval (Destructive Tool)** — posts the pending tool call and its parameters to a review channel for a human to approve or deny. 🔑\n- **Wait - For Approval Response** — pauses the run until an approver responds.\n- **IF - Approved?** — branches to execution if approved, else to a typed denial response with no production side effects."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "d2232df4-1869-48dd-bc4d-3a41626bda20",
      "name": "Sticky Note - Stage 3",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        2864,
        -304
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 5,
        "width": 1276,
        "height": 1228,
        "content": "## Stage 3: Narrow-Scoped Execution & Audit Log\n\n- **HTTP - Execute: Deploy Service** — calls the deploy API for exactly one named service/environment. 🔑\n- **HTTP - Execute: Query Production Database** — runs a pre-parameterized, read-only lookup against production data. 🔑\n- **HTTP - Execute: Search Knowledge Base** — queries an internal knowledge base or vector store for the requested query. 🔑\n- **HTTP - Execute: Issue Refund** — calls the payments API to issue a refund for a specific order/amount. 🔑\n- **Respond - Approval Denied** — returns a typed denial result with no side effects when a human rejects a destructive call.\n- **JS - Merge Execution Result** — normalizes whichever execution branch ran into one consistent result shape.\n- **JS - Log Call (Post-Execution)** — appends the outcome (success/failure, response) to the same audit trail row as the pre-execution log.\n- **Respond - Tool Result (Success)** — returns the tool's result back through the MCP Server Trigger to the calling MCP client."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
